    "title": "Bubble Sort: Adjacent Swaps",
    "subject": "Computer Science",
    "objective": "Show adjacent comparisons, swaps, and the growing sorted suffix.",
    "learner": "Can read a loop.",
    "misconceptions": ["One pass always sorts the whole array", "Bubble sort starts from the middle"],
    "expectedUnderstanding": [
      "Each comparison checks only an adjacent pair; a swap removes that local inversion.",
      "The largest remaining value reaches the right end after each full pass.",
      "The sorted suffix grows from the right, so later passes need fewer comparisons."
    ]
  },
