  "fallback": {
    "text": "Bubble sort scans left to right, comparing each adjacent pair. If the left value is larger, the two swap; otherwise nothing moves. After one full pass the largest value is at the right end. The next pass repeats only over the unsorted prefix, so the sorted suffix grows by one cell per pass. One pass does not generally sort everything: only the largest remaining value is guaranteed to be fixed. The scan always starts at the leftmost pair, never in the middle. If a full pass makes no swaps, the array is already sorted and the algorithm can stop."
  },
